{
  "title": "Thermopylae",
  "period": "480 BC",
  "summary": "After Herodotus: the Greeks hold a road squeezed between the mountain and the sea, until a mountain path lets the Persians come down behind them. The shoreline has since moved kilometres north, so the ancient sea is shown approximately.",
