  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "A road between the mountain and the sea",
      "text": "The Greeks chose to hold Thermopylae because it was narrow: a steep, impassable mountain on one side, the sea and marshes on the other, and in places room for only a single cart.\n\nToday the ground looks nothing like that. The cross-section from the mountain to the sea crosses kilometres of flat land: silt the Spercheios river has laid down since. The shaded sea shows roughly where the shore ran in 480 BC.",
      "focus": [
        "ancient-sea",
        "narrows",
        "phocian-wall",
        "anthela",
        "alpenoi"
      ],
      "camera": {
        "center": [22.52, 38.79],
        "zoom": 11.2
      },
      "analysis": {
        "type": "profile",
        "coords": [[22.535, 38.76], [22.535, 38.86]],
        "label": "From the mountain to today's coast, across the pass",
        "zh": {
          "label": "穿过关隘、从山到今日海岸的剖面"
        }
      },
      "zh": {
        "title": "山海之间的一条路",
        "text": "希腊人选择据守温泉关，因为它狭窄：一侧是陡峭难越的高山，另一侧是海和沼泽，有些地方只容一车通过。\n\n今天的地形已面目全非。从山到海的剖面横穿数公里平地：那是此后斯佩尔凯奥斯河冲积的泥沙。阴影所示的海大致是公元前480年的海岸位置。"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Two days of frontal attacks",
      "text": "Xerxes waited four days, then sent in the Medes and then his Immortals. In the narrow space their numbers were no use; the Spartans feigned flight, turned and cut down their pursuers. Two days of attacks along the road failed.",
      "focus": [
        "persian-front",
        "narrows",
        "phocian-wall",
        "trachis"
      ],
      "camera": {
        "center": [22.49, 38.8],
        "zoom": 12
      },
      "zh": {
        "title": "两天的正面进攻",
        "text": "薛西斯等了四天，先后派米底人和“不死军”进攻。在狭窄的地方，人多毫无用处；斯巴达人假装败退，再回身斩杀追兵。沿大道的两天进攻均告失败。"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "The path over the mountain",
      "text": "Ephialtes of Malis told Xerxes of a path: up the Asopos gorge, along the ridge of the mountain, and down at Alpenus, behind the Greeks. Hydarnes and the Immortals set out at nightfall and marched all night.\n\nThe comparison sets the path beside the road through the pass: a far longer, steeper way round, but one that ends behind the wall.",
      "focus": [
        "anopaea",
        "coast-road",
        "alpenoi"
      ],
      "analysis": {
        "type": "compare",
        "routes": [
          "anopaea",
          "coast-road"
        ],
        "label": "The Anopaea path vs the road through the pass",
        "zh": {
          "label": "阿诺佩亚小道与关隘大道比较"
        }
      },
      "zh": {
        "title": "翻山的小道",
        "text": "马利斯人厄菲阿尔特斯向薛西斯告密：有一条小道沿阿索波斯峡谷而上，循山脊而行，在希腊人后方的阿尔佩诺伊下山。许达尔涅斯率“不死军”在掌灯时分出发，走了整整一夜。\n\n比较把小道与关隘大道并列：绕路更远、更陡，但终点在城墙后面。"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Dawn on the summit",
      "text": "At dawn the Immortals reached the summit, where a thousand Phocians guarded the path. Hearing leaves trampled in the oak woods, the Phocians ran to arm and fell back to the top of the mountain, expecting to be attacked; the Persians ignored them and hurried down.\n\nThe line of sight from the wall to the summit shows that the defenders in the pass could not see what was happening up there.",
      "focus": [
        "anopaea",
        "phocian-post",
        "phocian-wall"
      ],
      "camera": {
        "center": [22.53, 38.775],
        "zoom": 12.2
      },
      "analysis": {
        "type": "los",
        "from": "phocian-wall",
